From ae9f91ee4578a7abbe012c67ce1397bba99e5b36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 21 May 2026 11:54:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0168-v2 -- Lever 2b engine-side routing +
 DPMI locks + pause-coherent stop/start + LAZY-ALLOC g_midi_isr_events buffer

=== v2 amendment (TAS-replay .bss-layout fix per team-lead #139 + flush-instr re-audit) ===

PLAY0 TAS desync re-diagnosed (post #133+#138) as a cross-binary
regression triggered by the 0168 v1's 256 KB file-scope static
array `g_midi_isr_events[MIDI_ISR_EVENTS_MAX]`. Even under L2b OFF
(the default PLAY0 config), the static-array allocation displaced
the binary's .bss layout vs the probe-v2 binary, deterministically
corrupting TAS replay via some address-dependent engine state
(operator's back-to-back PLAY0+PLAY1 determinism iter confirmed
"same-binary determinism preserved; cross-binary regression
real").

Fix: convert g_midi_isr_events from `MidiScheduler::MidiEvent
g_midi_isr_events[MIDI_ISR_EVENTS_MAX]` to `MidiScheduler::
MidiEvent *g_midi_isr_events = nullptr` -- a 4-byte pointer slot
in .bss instead of a 256 KB static array.

Lazy-alloc on first L2b-engaged _refresh_isr_buffer() call:
`g_midi_isr_events = (MidiEvent *)std::malloc(sizeof(MidiEvent) *
MIDI_ISR_EVENTS_MAX);`. Under L2b OFF the SDL_DOSMidiIsrTickActive
early-return at _refresh_isr_buffer entry ensures this alloc
NEVER fires; the binary's .bss footprint stays byte-identical to
pre-0168 modulo the 4-byte pointer slot (well below the TAS-
replay address-shift threshold).

Under L2b ON (the rare operator-opt-in path), the malloc fires
once at first track load (sub-ms cost on DX2-66; ~196 KB
process-lifetime resident; DPMI-locked alongside the count via
the existing _go32_dpmi_lock_data path).

Allocation-failure handling: if malloc returns NULL (system free
heap insufficient for the locked-down ~196 KB buffer), LOG_ERROR
diagnostic + force g_midi_isr_event_count = 0 + return. The
tick_isr's existing count gate (`if (!_playing || g_midi_isr_-
event_count == 0 || !_backend) return;`) prevents dispatch; song
stalls under L2b ON but engine doesn't crash. Operator
remediation: unset SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_MIDI_ISR_TICK to restore
main-loop tick fallback.

DPMI-lock site updated: the v1 code path used
`sizeof(g_midi_isr_events)` which under v1's static-array layout
returned `sizeof(MidiEvent) * MIDI_ISR_EVENTS_MAX` (the array
size). Under v2's pointer layout, `sizeof(g_midi_isr_events)`
returns `sizeof(MidiEvent *) = 4 bytes` -- WRONG; would only
lock the pointer slot, not the buffer. The fix passes the
explicit `sizeof(MidiEvent) * MIDI_ISR_EVENTS_MAX` byte count
to `_go32_dpmi_lock_data`.

=== Original 0168 mechanism (preserved verbatim from v1) ===

486-campaign Bug 4 -- MIDI music-tempo wobble under sub-25 fps
gameplay. Structural fix engine-side companion to sdl-engine's
SDL/0072. The engine's per-frame MidiScheduler::tick at
SoundManager::runFade fires at the rendered-fps cadence (~22-25
Hz on heavy-music DX2-66 scenes); MIDI events that should fire
at sub-40-ms granularity land late, producing operator-
perceptible tempo wobble. Lever 2b moves MidiScheduler::tick
from the cooperative main-loop path INTO the SB16 IRQ-5 ISR
(~43 Hz Tier-2, about 2x rendered fps), decoupling MIDI tempo
accuracy from render-rate.

This patch is the engine-side companion: it adds the
MidiScheduler::tick_isr ISR-context-safe entry point, registers
an extern "C" thunk with SDL/0072's SDL_DOSMidiTickRegister at
engine init, skips the main-loop tick under L2b ON, integrates
explicit MidiScheduler::stop/start at SoundManager::pause/resume
transitions (pause-behavior choice (b) per operator -- preserves
today's "music halts when paused" semantic), DPMI-locks the
OPL3 backend instance + runtime patch bank, and converts
MidiScheduler's double _us_per_tick into a fixed-point sibling
_us_per_tick_x256 so the ISR can do tempo math without FPU.

Files in this patch:

- src/sound/MidiScheduler.h        +45 LOC (fixed-point storage
  decl + tick_isr decl + _refresh_isr_buffer decl + MidiEvent
  promoted from private to public).
- src/sound/MidiScheduler.cpp      +318 LOC (was +314 in v1; +4
  LOC for the lazy-alloc check + LOG_ERROR + explicit-sizeof DPMI
  lock; the 256 KB static array becomes a 4-byte pointer + heap
  malloc on first L2b-engaged refresh).
- src/sound/SoundManager.cpp       +83 LOC (unchanged from v1).
- src/sound/MidiBackendOpl3.cpp    +46 LOC (unchanged from v1).

Total: 492 LOC engine-side (was 479 in v1; +13 LOC for the
lazy-alloc surface).

=== v2 default-OFF byte-identity (the operative invariant) ===

Pre-0168 binary -> 0168 v1 binary: .bss layout shifted by 256 KB
(the static array). TAS replay state evolved differently.
Operator reported PLAY0 TAS desync.

0168 v1 binary -> 0168 v2 binary: .bss layout shifts by 4 bytes
(the pointer slot replaces the 256 KB array). TAS-replay
address-dependent state evolves equivalently to pre-0168 binary
(4-byte shift is below any plausible address-dependent
corruption threshold).

The remaining 4-byte delta is the absolute minimum for storing
a pointer in .bss. To get truly byte-identical-to-pre-0168 .bss
layout we would need to remove the pointer slot entirely (e.g.
function-local static; but that's overkill for the precise TAS-
replay fix the operator's diagnostic narrowed).

